ENTRY            23623   20251211   20260826   20260826       2323
SUBENT        23623001   20251211   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                 17         78
TITLE      Measurements of neutron capture cross-sections for
           nuclides of interest in decommissioning (IV) :
           165Ho(n, gamma) 166m, 166gHo reactions
AUTHOR     (S.Nakamura,Y.Shibahara,S.Endo,G.Rovira,A.Kimura)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNJAE,2JPNKTO)
REFERENCE  (J,NST,62,1086,2025)
           #doi:10.1080/00223131.2025.2525327
FACILITY   (REAC,2JPNKTO)
           Kyoto University Research Reactor (KUR) .
INC-SOURCE (REAC)The thermal column pneumatic tube (TC-Pn) in
           KUR. The nominal neutron flux intensity of TC-Pn is
           2.84E+11 (n/cm2/sec) at 5 MW power operation.
           The AUTHORs confirmed that the TC-Pn was well
           thermalized in the previous experiment.
           See Fig. 9 in J,NST,58,1061,2021 (REL-REF) .
METHOD     (ACTIV,GSPEC) Based on Westcott convention formula.
           Samples and monitors were irradiated in the TC-Pn for
           6 hours under 5-MW power operation. The decay
           gamma-rays were measured with a high-purity germanium
           detector.
                      Cooling Time  Measurement Time
           Ho-166g:      7 days       40 hours
           Ho-166m:     119 days     7.5 days
SAMPLE     Two identical metal Ho samples were prepared and the
           irradiation and the measurement were performed with
           the two samples together.
           Sample:    Ho-nat metal foils
                        1.578+-0.001 mg and 1.545+-0.001 mg
           Monitor:   Co-59:  Co-nat metal foil 0.469+-0.001 mg
                      Mo-98:  Mo-nat metal foil 1.415+-0.001 mg
                      Au-197: Au/Al Alloy wire  0.615+-0.001 mg
DETECTOR   (HPGE) High purity germanium detector, relative
           efficiency of 25%.
           The gamma-ray peak efficiencies of the Ge detector
           were measured using a Eu-152 source and a mixed source
           of Cs-137 and Co-60.
           The uncertainty in the source radioactivity was 1.5%
           for both of the standard sources.
ANALYSIS   The reaction rates of the target reactions were
           obtained from the yields of the gamma rays emitted
           from the irradiated samples.
           Because the neutron flux in the TC-Pn is well
           thermalized, epithermal component in Westcott
           convention method was negligibly small.
           The thermal-neutron flux was derived using neutron
           flux monitors: Au-197, Co-59 and Mo-98. The obtained
           neutron flux was (2.684+-0.015)E+11 (n/cm2/sec) .
           The capture cross sections were derived using the
           reaction rates and the thermal-neutron flux.
           The thermal capture cross sections for monitors and
           the g-factors were taken from REL-REF.
CORRECTION Self-shielding effect for thermal neutrons and decay
           gamma-rays were corrected.
DECAY-DATA The half-lives and emission probabilities for samples
           and monitors were taken from Nucleide-Lara.
           (67-HO-166-G,26.808HR,DG,1379.45,0.00905)
           (67-HO-166-M,1133.YR,DG,184.41,0.725,
                                DG,280.46,0.2954,
                                DG,711.68,0.549,
                                DG,810.28,0.573)
           (27-CO-60-G,5.2711YR,DG,1173.24,0.9985,
                                DG,1332.49,0.99826)
           (42-MO-99,2.7479D,DG,739.50,0.1212)
           (79-AU-198-G,2.6943D,DG,411.80,0.9562)
ASSUMED    Thermal capture cross sections of the monitors were
           assumed to determine the thermal neutron flux.
           (ASSUM1,27-CO-59(N,G)27-CO-60,,SIG)
           (ASSUM2,42-MO-98(N,G)42-MO-99,,SIG)
           (ASSUM3,79-AU-197(N,G)79-AU-198,,SIG)
ERR-ANALYS (ASSUM1-ERR) Uncertainty of Co-59 thermal C.S.
           (ASSUM2-ERR) Uncertainty of Mo-98 thermal C.S.
           (ASSUM3-ERR) Uncertainty of Au-197 thermal C.S.
REL-REF    (R,,S.F.Mughabghab,B,NEUT.RES,,,2018) Thermal capture
           cross section of the monitors and g-factor were given.
           (I,,S.Nakamura+,J,NST,58,1061,2021) The reference to
           show that the irradiation field is well thermalized.
STATUS     (APRVD) Proofread by Shoji Nakamura. (2025-12-11)
HISTORY    (20251211C) By A.Kimura.
ENDBIB              78
